WEBVTT

00:00:00.114 --> 00:00:03.857
A deployed RAG application needs more than a working notebook.

00:00:03.857 --> 00:00:12.107
Logging should capture the user question, retrieved chunk IDs, scores, model response, latency,

00:00:12.107 --> 00:00:14.542
and useful feedback signals.

00:00:14.542 --> 00:00:20.892
Cost monitoring may include embedding calls, vector database usage, reranking, and language-model tokens.

00:00:20.892 --> 00:00:27.402
Governance includes access control, source freshness, data retention,

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:31.482
and human review for sensitive use cases.

00:00:31.482 --> 00:00:36.402
The indexing pipeline needs scheduled or event-driven updates.

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:40.817
The system also needs evaluation over time.

00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:47.162
A model upgrade, embedding change, chunking change, or new document collection can affect retrieval quality.

00:00:47.162 --> 00:00:52.002
Think of RAG as both a data system and an AI system.

00:00:52.002 --> 00:00:57.902
The language model is only one service in a larger pipeline.

00:00:57.902 --> 00:01:04.477
Companies operate the entire pipeline, so observability and maintenance are part of the architecture.
